  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Arroz de pato is a two-stage dish. First you "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "braise",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "braise"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " duck legs in white wine and stock until the meat falls away from the bone, "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "resting",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "resting"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " while the braising liquid becomes the base for the rice. Then everything bakes together with crispy chorizo on top."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Use exactly 700ml of braising liquid for the rice. Too much and it goes mushy; too little and it burns."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
