      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Method"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "orderedList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Heat oil in dutch oven. Brown duck or chicken thighs all over. Remove."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Soften onion and garlic in the same pot for 5 minutes."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Return meat. Add wine, stock, bay leaves, and thyme. Bring to a simmer. Cover. Cook for 1 hour until very tender."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Remove meat. Shred off the bones. Reserve the braising liquid."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Measure 700ml of braising liquid. Bring to the boil. Add rice. Cook until nearly tender and liquid is almost absorbed."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Heat oven to 200C."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Mix shredded meat through rice. Add lemon zest and seasoning."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Spread rice in an oven dish. Lay chorizo slices on top."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Bake for 20 minutes until chorizo is crisp and top is golden. Scatter parsley and squeeze lemon juice before serving."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "troubleshooter",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "troubleshooterItem",
            "attrs": {
              "symptom": "Rice is mushy",
              "cause": "Too much liquid or overcooked before baking",
              "fix": "Use exactly 700ml of braising liquid and stop cooking when liquid is almost absorbed."
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "troubleshooterItem",
            "attrs": {
              "symptom": "Top not crisp",
              "cause": "Oven too low or not enough time",
              "fix": "Switch to the grill for the last 5 minutes."
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "troubleshooterItem",
            "attrs": {
              "symptom": "Meat tough",
              "cause": "Not braised long enough",
              "fix": "Cook the full hour. Chicken thighs need at least 45 minutes."
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Where this dish lives"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Arroz de pato is considered one of Portugal's great dishes. The Alentejo region claims it, though it is eaten all over the country. The rice cooked in duck stock is the heart of the dish, and no braising liquid is ever wasted. It appears at Christmas tables and Sunday lunches across Portugal. The combination of citrus and cured pork with rich dark meat is a defining flavour pattern in Portuguese cooking."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
